# How to cite pyharnx. GitHub reads this file for the repository's
# "Cite this repository" button, which offers it as APA and BibTeX.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use pyharnx in your research, please cite it as below.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
# The concept DOI, which resolves to the latest version Zenodo has archived.
# Each release also gets a DOI of its own, on its Zenodo record.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24283575
title: "pyharnx: a minimal agent harness in Python, built for experiments"
abstract: >-
  A minimal agent harness in Python, built for experiments, and a lightweight
  alternative to pi: small enough to read in an afternoon, with one agentic
  loop across vendors, every step a typed event, and every request
  reproducible from its transcript.
authors:
  - given-names: Liyan
    family-names: Xu
repository-code: https://github.com/lxucs/pyharnx
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agents
  - llm
  - agent harness
  - experiments
  - research
  - reproducibility
